{
  "id": "ss.char.prism",
  "name": "Prism",
  "description": "A survivor cut to a facet — the cicada of the eight. The chest plate is two planes meeting on a ridge, one lit and one in shade, and the helmet is the same diamond it always was, worn as a face. Two long clear wings lie folded down the back from the shoulders to the hip, and on the flank under the near arm sits a ribbed tymbal: the drum a cicada sings with, and the one thing this body still makes a sound with. It chirps — a hum thrown outward in a ring — and the ring is drawn leaving the drum in the idle, faint and cold, because it is a sound and not a scent. The feelers are held wide, one thrown forward and one back, the widest spread on the roster: this is the survivor that finds things. Long light legs, because it is also the one that runs. Same dead organ as the rest, same place. Bare chitin cold slate, pink plate over it. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
